{
  "id": "ch4",
  "title": "THE SINK",
  "objPage": "S8A1",
  "preset": "drowned",
  "notes": [
    "COHERENCE (2026-10-22): ch4 goes down into the Sink, Fessenden's drowned underworld, in one direction: a0 THE SINK is the flooded street at the rim (E1a2 176-848 only: the broken brick wall over the drowned city, floodwater over the pavement), a1 THE PUMP STATION is the pump hall below it (E4a2 0-1024 only: the grated floor under the hall's own far layer of pipes, pressure globes and vats, the vats' red liquid turned to floodwater), a2 THE DIG is the excavation in Fessenden's flooded caves (E8a2 1792-2816 only: the cave arches, raised water, scaffold timbers and pump risers). Each area walks back and forth through its one source strip (legs <= 512 px, leftward legs mirrored), so every join is a mirror join or a continuation; the place changes only at the fades.",
    "Palette: the drowned preset (flood + ruin + night 0.8, lifted 1.45 in lightness) in the pump hall; the street and the caves take a damp teal tint (hue -12..-15, saturation 0.7-0.8, 22% toward #2a5a5a / #1a3a3a) that keeps their brick and rock readable; the standing water is E8a1's harbor water (palette row 4) darkened to murky teal.",
    "a2 is the chapter's return visit (ARCHITECTURE §3.8): Fessenden's caves six months on, flooded and dug out by Cinder's crews; >= 25% of its cells are patched (the floodwater over the cave floor, scaffold timbers, pump risers).",
    "Boss arena (4-6, FOREMAN CINDER, the salvage diver with the pile driver): the dig's pump house: pump risers with their elbows (E7a3 816-912, palette row 4 lifted) between scaffold timbers (the E6a0 portal timber, rows 9/8/3/2 lifted) over the flooded floor; the runtime adds the pump columns (props) and the vent cycles."
  ],
